title Model Context Protocol (MCP) - Complete End-to-End Lifecycle

start

partition "**MCP ARCHITECTURE OVERVIEW**" {

:**MCP System Components**
----
**Core Components:**

**1. MCP SERVER**
* Exposes resources and capabilities
* Implements MCP protocol
* Manages context and tools
* Handles requests from clients
* Types:
  - Resource servers (data/content)
  - Tool servers (functions/actions)
  - Prompt servers (templates)
  - Hybrid servers (multiple types)

**2. MCP CLIENT**
* Connects to MCP servers
* Discovers available resources
* Makes requests to servers
* Receives and processes responses
* Typically integrated in:
  - AI applications
  - Chat interfaces
  - IDEs (Claude Desktop, VS Code)
  - Development tools

**3. MCP PROTOCOL**
* JSON-RPC 2.0 based
* Transport layers:
  - stdio (Standard I/O)
  - HTTP/SSE (Server-Sent Events)
  - WebSocket (future)
* Message types:
  - Requests
  - Responses
  - Notifications

**4. RESOURCES**
* Data/content exposed by server
* Types:
  - Text resources
  - File resources
  - Database queries
  - API data
  - Dynamic content
* URI-based addressing

**5. TOOLS**
* Functions/actions server provides
* Executable capabilities
* Input schemas (JSON Schema)
* Output format definitions

**6. PROMPTS**
* Reusable prompt templates
* Dynamic arguments
* Context injection
* Template variables;

}

partition "**SERVER DEVELOPMENT**" {

:**1. Server Setup & Initialization**
----
**Create MCP Server:**

* Choose implementation:
  - TypeScript/JavaScript SDK
  - Python SDK
  - Custom implementation

* Install MCP SDK:
  - npm install @modelcontextprotocol/sdk
  - pip install mcp

* Initialize server instance
* Configure server metadata:
  - Name
  - Version
  - Description
  - Capabilities

* Set up transport:
  - stdio transport
  - HTTP/SSE transport
  - Custom transport

**Example Structure:**
* Server class initialization
* Protocol version: 2024-11-05
* Implementation info
* Capability declarations;

:**2. Resource Registration**
----
**Define & Register Resources:**

* Create resource definitions:
  - Resource URI scheme
  - Resource metadata
  - Content types (MIME)
  - Access patterns

* Implement resource handlers:
  - List resources (discovery)
  - Read resource (fetch content)
  - Subscribe to updates (optional)
  - Resource templates

**Resource Types:**
* **Static Resources**
  - Files
  - Documents
  - Configuration data

* **Dynamic Resources**
  - Database queries
  - API results
  - Computed data
  - Real-time data

**Resource Schema:**
* URI: resource://server/path
* Name: Display name
* Description: Purpose
* MIME type: Content format
* Metadata: Additional info;

:**3. Tool Registration**
----
**Define & Register Tools:**

* Create tool definitions:
  - Tool name (unique ID)
  - Description (what it does)
  - Input schema (JSON Schema)
  - Output format

* Implement tool handlers:
  - Parse input parameters
  - Validate inputs
  - Execute tool logic
  - Return structured output
  - Handle errors

**Tool Types:**
* **Data Tools**
  - Query databases
  - Search files
  - Fetch APIs
  - Read sensors

* **Action Tools**
  - Write files
  - Send emails
  - Make API calls
  - Execute commands

* **Computation Tools**
  - Calculate values
  - Transform data
  - Analyze content
  - Generate reports

**Input Schema Example:**
* type: object
* properties: parameters
* required: mandatory fields
* descriptions: field help;

:**4. Prompt Registration**
----
**Define & Register Prompts:**

* Create prompt templates:
  - Prompt name
  - Description
  - Template text
  - Dynamic arguments
  - Argument schemas

* Implement prompt handlers:
  - Accept arguments
  - Generate prompt
  - Insert variables
  - Return formatted prompt

**Prompt Features:**
* Variable substitution
* Conditional sections
* Context injection
* Multi-turn templates
* System instructions;

:**5. Capability Declaration**
----
**Declare Server Capabilities:**

* **Resources Capability**
  - supports: true/false
  - listChanged: notification support
  - subscribe: subscription support

* **Tools Capability**
  - supports: true/false
  - Available tools count

* **Prompts Capability**
  - supports: true/false
  - Available prompts count

* **Logging Capability**
  - supports: true/false
  - Log levels supported

* **Sampling Capability**
  - supports: true/false
  - LLM sampling support

Document all capabilities
Version compatibility;

:**6. Server Configuration**
----
* Set up environment variables
* Configure credentials/API keys
* Set resource paths
* Configure rate limits
* Set timeout values
* Configure logging
* Define error handling
* Set security policies
* Configure CORS (if HTTP)
* Set up authentication;

:**7. Server Startup**
----
* Initialize transport layer
* Start listening for connections
* Register signal handlers
* Set up graceful shutdown
* Log server ready state
* Publish server metadata
* Wait for client connections
* Monitor server health;

}

partition "**CLIENT INTEGRATION**" {

:**8. Client Setup**
----
**Initialize MCP Client:**

* Install MCP client SDK
* Create client instance
* Configure client settings:
  - Client name
  - Client version
  - Timeout settings
  - Retry policies

* Set up transport connection:
  - stdio (subprocess)
  - HTTP/SSE endpoint
  - Connection parameters

* Initialize client capabilities:
  - Roots (workspace roots)
  - Sampling (LLM access)
  - Notifications;

:**9. Server Discovery & Connection**
----
**Connect to MCP Server:**

* Configure server connection:
  - Server command (for stdio)
  - Server URL (for HTTP)
  - Environment variables
  - Working directory

* Establish connection:
  - Start server process (stdio)
  - HTTP handshake
  - Protocol negotiation

* Exchange initialization:
  - Send initialize request
  - Server returns capabilities
  - Client acknowledges
  - Send initialized notification

* Store server connection
* Log connection status;

:**10. Capability Negotiation**
----
**Exchange Capabilities:**

* **Client sends initialize:**
  - protocolVersion
  - clientInfo (name, version)
  - capabilities:
    * roots (list)
    * sampling (LLM access)
    * experimental features

* **Server responds:**
  - protocolVersion
  - serverInfo (name, version)
  - capabilities:
    * resources
    * tools
    * prompts
    * logging
    * sampling
  - instructions (optional)

* Store negotiated capabilities
* Validate compatibility
* Enable/disable features;

:**11. Server Discovery**
----
**Discover Available Resources:**

* **List Resources:**
  - Send resources/list request
  - Receive resource list
  - Store resource metadata:
    * URI
    * Name
    * Description
    * MIME type
    * Annotations

* **List Tools:**
  - Send tools/list request
  - Receive tool list
  - Store tool metadata:
    * Name
    * Description
    * Input schema

* **List Prompts:**
  - Send prompts/list request
  - Receive prompt list
  - Store prompt metadata:
    * Name
    * Description
    * Arguments

* Cache discovered items
* Update UI/interface
* Enable user selection;

}

partition "**RUNTIME OPERATIONS**" {

:**12. User Request**
----
* User submits query/command
* Parse user intent
* Identify required resources:
  - Context needed
  - Tools to use
  - Prompts to apply
* Determine MCP operations
* Plan execution sequence;

:**13. Resource Reading**
----
**Read Resource Content:**

* **Build Request:**
  - Method: resources/read
  - params:
    * uri: resource URI
    * additional options

* **Send Request:**
  - JSON-RPC request
  - Request ID
  - Transport to server

* **Receive Response:**
  - contents array:
    * uri
    * mimeType
    * text or blob
  - metadata

* **Process Content:**
  - Parse based on MIME type
  - Extract relevant data
  - Store in context
  - Handle errors

* Cache resource content
* Update access timestamp;

:**14. Tool Execution**
----
**Execute Server Tool:**

* **Prepare Tool Call:**
  - Tool name
  - Input parameters (validated)
  - JSON Schema compliance

* **Build Request:**
  - Method: tools/call
  - params:
    * name: tool name
    * arguments: parameters object

* **Send Request:**
  - JSON-RPC request
  - Set timeout
  - Transport to server

* **Server Processing:**
  - Validate inputs
  - Execute tool logic
  - Generate output
  - Format response

* **Receive Response:**
  - content array:
    * type: text/image/resource
    * text/data/uri
  - isError: boolean
  - tool execution metadata

* **Handle Result:**
  - Parse tool output
  - Integrate into workflow
  - Log execution
  - Handle errors;

:**15. Prompt Generation**
----
**Get Prompt from Server:**

* **Build Request:**
  - Method: prompts/get
  - params:
    * name: prompt name
    * arguments: dynamic args

* **Send Request:**
  - JSON-RPC request
  - Include argument values

* **Server Processing:**
  - Load prompt template
  - Substitute variables
  - Inject context
  - Format prompt

* **Receive Response:**
  - description: prompt purpose
  - messages array:
    * role: system/user/assistant
    * content: text/image/resource
  - formatted prompt

* **Use Prompt:**
  - Send to LLM
  - Include in conversation
  - Apply to task;

:**16. Sampling (LLM Requests)**
----
**Server Requests LLM Completion:**

* **Server sends sampling/createMessage:**
  - messages: conversation history
  - modelPreferences:
    * hints (suggested models)
    * costPriority
    * speedPriority
    * intelligencePriority
  - systemPrompt
  - includeContext
  - temperature
  - maxTokens
  - stopSequences
  - metadata

* **Client Processing:**
  - Select appropriate LLM
  - Build LLM request
  - Include context
  - Send to LLM API

* **LLM Response:**
  - Generated text
  - Token usage
  - Finish reason

* **Client Returns:**
  - model: used model
  - role: assistant
  - content: generated text
  - stopReason
  - usage metrics

* Server continues processing
* Enables server-driven LLM use;

:**17. Context Assembly**
----
**Combine All Context:**

* Collect from multiple sources:
  - Resource content (MCP)
  - Tool outputs (MCP)
  - Prompt templates (MCP)
  - Conversation history
  - User preferences
  - System context

* Structure context:
  - Prioritize by relevance
  - Order logically
  - Format consistently
  - Add metadata

* Manage context size:
  - Token counting
  - Truncation strategy
  - Compression
  - Summarization

* Prepare for LLM;

:**18. LLM Request**
----
**Send to Language Model:**

* Build final prompt:
  - System instructions
  - MCP context (resources)
  - Tool descriptions
  - User query
  - Conversation history

* Configure LLM parameters:
  - Model selection
  - Temperature
  - Max tokens
  - Top-p
  - Stop sequences

* Send API request
* Handle streaming (optional)
* Monitor token usage
* Track costs;

:**19. Response Processing**
----
* Receive LLM output
* Parse response
* Extract:
  - Answer text
  - Tool calls (if any)
  - Citations
  - Reasoning

* Validate response
* Check for tool invocations
* Process structured outputs;

if (Tool Call\nRequested?) then (Yes)
  :Parse Tool Call;
  :Execute via MCP;
  note right
    Loop back to step 14
    for tool execution
  end note
  detach
else (No)
endif

:**20. Response Enhancement**
----
* Add MCP resource citations
* Link to source URIs
* Include tool outputs
* Format with context
* Add metadata:
  - Resources used
  - Tools invoked
  - Prompts applied
  - Server sources
* Structure final response;

:**21. Response Delivery**
----
* Format for user
* Include citations
* Show resource links
* Display tool results
* Add interactive elements
* Send to user interface
* Log interaction;

}

partition "**NOTIFICATIONS & UPDATES**" {

:**22. Server Notifications**
----
**Handle Server Events:**

* **Resource List Changed:**
  - Notification: notifications/resources/list_changed
  - Refresh resource list
  - Update UI

* **Tool List Changed:**
  - Notification: notifications/tools/list_changed
  - Refresh tool list
  - Update capabilities

* **Prompt List Changed:**
  - Notification: notifications/prompts/list_changed
  - Refresh prompt list

* **Progress Notifications:**
  - Notification: notifications/progress
  - Progress token
  - Progress value
  - Update UI indicators

* **Log Messages:**
  - Notification: notifications/message
  - level: debug/info/warning/error
  - logger: source
  - data: message
  - Log to console/file

* Handle asynchronously
* Update client state
* Refresh caches;

:**23. Client Notifications**
----
**Send to Server:**

* **Roots Changed:**
  - Notification: notifications/roots/list_changed
  - New workspace roots
  - Server updates context

* **Cancellation:**
  - Notification: notifications/cancelled
  - requestId: cancelled request
  - reason: cancellation reason
  - Server stops processing

* Send asynchronously
* No response expected;

}

partition "**ERROR HANDLING & RESILIENCE**" {

:**24. Error Handling**
----
**Handle MCP Errors:**

* **Connection Errors:**
  - Server unreachable
  - Connection timeout
  - Transport failure
  - Retry strategy
  - Fallback options

* **Protocol Errors:**
  - Invalid message format
  - Unsupported method
  - Protocol version mismatch
  - Capability mismatch

* **Request Errors:**
  - Invalid parameters
  - Resource not found
  - Tool execution failure
  - Permission denied
  - Rate limit exceeded

* **Response Errors:**
  - error code
  - error message
  - error data
  - Parse and handle
  - Log details

* Display user-friendly messages
* Retry if appropriate
* Fallback mechanisms
* Circuit breaker pattern;

:**25. Connection Management**
----
* Monitor connection health
* Implement heartbeat/ping
* Detect disconnections
* Automatic reconnection:
  - Exponential backoff
  - Maximum retry attempts
  - Connection pooling
* Handle server restarts
* Maintain session state
* Graceful degradation;

:**26. Resource Management**
----
* Manage open connections
* Clean up resources:
  - Close unused connections
  - Clear caches
  - Release file handles
  - Free memory
* Implement timeouts
* Handle memory limits
* Monitor resource usage
* Apply rate limiting;

}

partition "**SECURITY & COMPLIANCE**" {

:**27. Authentication & Authorization**
----
**Security Measures:**

* **Authentication:**
  - API keys
  - OAuth tokens
  - Certificates
  - Environment variables
  - Secure credential storage

* **Authorization:**
  - Resource access control
  - Tool permission checks
  - Role-based access (RBAC)
  - Capability-based security

* **Data Protection:**
  - Encrypt in transit (TLS)
  - Encrypt at rest
  - Sanitize inputs
  - Validate outputs
  - PII protection

* **Network Security:**
  - CORS policies (HTTP)
  - IP whitelisting
  - Request signing
  - Rate limiting

* Audit logging
* Compliance tracking;

:**28. Input Validation**
----
* Validate all inputs:
  - JSON Schema validation
  - Parameter type checking
  - Range validation
  - Format verification
  - Injection prevention

* Sanitize inputs:
  - Remove malicious code
  - Escape special chars
  - Normalize data

* Apply security policies
* Log validation failures;

:**29. Monitoring & Observability**
----
**Track System Health:**

* **Performance Metrics:**
  - Request latency
  - Response time
  - Throughput
  - Success/error rates
  - Resource usage

* **Usage Metrics:**
  - Requests per server
  - Most used resources
  - Most used tools
  - Active connections
  - Token consumption

* **Health Metrics:**
  - Server availability
  - Connection stability
  - Error patterns
  - Timeout rates

* **Logging:**
  - Structured logs
  - Request/response logs
  - Error logs
  - Audit trails
  - Debug traces

* Set up dashboards
* Configure alerts
* Generate reports;

:**30. Continuous Improvement**
----
* Analyze usage patterns
* Identify bottlenecks
* Optimize performance:
  - Cache frequently used resources
  - Batch similar requests
  - Optimize tool execution
  - Improve prompt templates

* Update server capabilities
* Add new resources/tools
* Refine prompts
* Update documentation
* Version management
* Monitor compatibility;

}

