note right
  **MCP Protocol Basics:**
  
  **Transport Layers:**
  * stdio: Process communication
  * HTTP+SSE: Web-based
  * (Future: WebSocket)
  
  **Message Format:**
  * JSON-RPC 2.0
  * Request: method + params + id
  * Response: result/error + id
  * Notification: method + params
  
  **Core Methods:**
  * initialize / initialized
  * resources/list
  * resources/read
  * resources/subscribe
  * tools/list
  * tools/call
  * prompts/list
  * prompts/get
  * sampling/createMessage
  * logging/setLevel
  
  **Key Features:**
  * Bidirectional communication
  * Server-driven LLM sampling
  * Dynamic resource discovery
  * Tool orchestration
  * Prompt templating
  * Progress tracking
  * Notification system
  
  **Common Use Cases:**
  * IDE integration (VS Code)
  * Chat applications (Claude)
  * Development tools
  * Data access layers
  * API aggregation
  * Multi-tool orchestration
end note

